<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Windsor, Vermont</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Windsor is a town in Vermont on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut-river">Connecticut River</a>, known as the birthplace of Vermont. In July 1777 a convention meeting in a tavern there adopted the constitution of the independent Vermont Republic, the first in America to ban adult <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>. Vermont joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in 1791.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/windsor-vermont.jpg" alt="Windsor, Vermont" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ascended Dreamer · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Windsor_VT_2-07-2026.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
